        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-chat-202611100526-00e424b1aafd",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, take a bus to Colca Canyon.\n\nThe canyon is about **3,500 meters** deep. The activity of two nearby active volcanoes is thought to have helped shape this landscape.\n\nThe route includes several stops at viewpoints.\n\nYou may see pink flamingos at **Lagunillas Lake**.\n\nA tea stop at **Canchis** restaurant is planned to help you acclimatize.\n\nAnother viewpoint offers a panorama of three volcanoes.\n\nAt the end of the day, arrive in **Chivay** and check in at the three-star **Colca Llacta** hotel.\n\nYou can visit the hot springs if you wish. Time is set aside for lunch."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_label:73093f4feeb380dc",
      "field": "itinerary.label",
      "sourceTextSha256": "93918da548154ed9157a2b3f63138aadbebf123c03985f778e93de1ce9d23f3b",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-chat-202611100526-00e424b1aafd",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Puno and Lake Titicaca"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_alt:ba8229a8cdafb8a1",
      "field": "media.alt",
      "sourceTextSha256": "cb3be71933c945b52ee8aa4e39e4584af02a7e18d82867c9cb9c40613233d92b",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-chat-202611100526-00e424b1aafd",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "A reed boat beside an island with huts and people in brightly colored clothes in Puno, Peru"
    },
